+# Q3 2026 operating brief
+
+## Executive summary
+
+Q3 was a financially solid quarter: revenue of $720,000 against spend of
+$464,000 produced an operating surplus of $256,000. Support handled a high
+volume of tickets, closing 93.7% of the 1,250 opened during the quarter.
+The Q3 delivery plan kicked off on 2026-10-05 and, accounting for the
+company holiday on 2026-10-12, is on track to launch 2026-10-23. Security
+resolved 95.0% of the 80 incidents detected, holding steady against
+target. Overall, a healthy quarter across finance, support, delivery, and
+security — see Notes below for data-quality issues surfaced while
+compiling this brief.
+
+## Key figures
+
+| Metric | Value |
+|---|---:|
+| Q3 revenue | $720,000 |
+| Q3 spend | $464,000 |
+| Operating surplus | $256,000 |
+| Support close rate | 93.7% |
+| Launch date | 2026-10-23 |
+| Security resolution rate | 95.0% |
+
+## Notes
+
+While compiling this brief, the headline figures quoted in three of the
+four source packets did not match their own underlying tabulated data.
+This brief uses the figures recomputed from source data; leadership may
+want to flag the discrepancy to the owning teams as a possible reporting
+pipeline issue:
+
+- **Finance**: the itemized spend table (payroll, infrastructure,
+  contractors, facilities) sums to $464,000, which is $750 higher than the
+  $463,250 figure stated in the finance packet's summary sentence.
+- **Support**: ticket counts (1,171 closed of 1,250 opened) compute to a
+  93.7% close rate, versus the 96.4% quoted on the support dashboard.
+- **Delivery**: walking the phase durations as inclusive business days from
+  the 2026-10-05 start — and correctly excluding the 2026-10-12 company
+  holiday from the Build phase — yields a launch date of 2026-10-23, one
+  business day later than the 2026-10-22 date quoted in the delivery
+  summary.
+- **Security**: the quoted 95.0% resolution rate (76 of 80 incidents) does
+  check out against the underlying counts — no discrepancy found here.
+
+Given three out of four packets had summary/data mismatches, it may be
+worth a quick audit of how these dashboard summaries are generated.
